## 1. Three official guides already point at the same artefact

This is not an invented crossover. **Three** curricula already converge on a digital fashion showroom — from opposite sides of the stack:

| | **Creación Digital I–II** (Universidad Europea) | **Front-End I–II** (UDIT) | **Diseño de Moda** (UDIT) |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Degree | Grado en **Comunicación y Gestión de Moda** | Desarrollo Full-Stack · Ciencia de Datos e IA | **Graduado/a en Diseño de Moda / Bachelor in Fashion Design** (RUCT `2504586`, BOE-A-2024-1046) |
| Placement | **Year 1** — S1 and S2 · 6 ECTS each | FE I **Year 2 annual**; FE II **Year 3 S1** · 6 ECTS each | Full 4-year design degree; digital + project spine below |
| Relevant official contents | CD I: *"Fundamentos y representación de la forma tridimensional. Volumen."* · CD II: **"Creación de avatares"**, **"Diseño de experiencias de moda digitales"**, **"Maquetación, edición y creación de web y portfolio digital"**, **"Hologramas y R.A"** | FE II: arquitecturas, PWA, testing, rendimiento, **R3F/WebGL**, **shaders**, **IoT/servicios Python** | **Diseño digital I–II** (Y2) · **Proyectos I–IV** (annual) · **Tecnología Textil I–IV** · **Portfolio** (Y4 S1, 3 ECTS) · **Estilismo y Dirección Artística** · **Comunicación y Crítica** · TFG |
| Authoring tool in studio practice | avatars / digital experiences (guide-level) | the web runtime | **CLO 3D** — institutional studio practice for garment authoring (not named in the BOE subject list; treat as first-hand practice knowledge, same epistemic status as the Back-End II synergy sheet) |

**CD II is officially required to produce web and digital portfolio work, and 3D avatars, and AR.** FE II is officially required to teach 3D interfaces on the web. **Diseño de Moda** already runs a digital-design + proyectos + portfolio spine whose studio output is authored in CLO 3D. The three curricula point at the same artefact from *communication*, *interface engineering*, and *garment design*. The synergy makes each subject *more* compliant with its own guide, not less.

**One methodology across the triangle:** the same critical, AI-assisted, docs-first paradigm — *another way of the tao, but the tao is one and many*. The professor owns FE + CD; Fashion Design joins as **content authors and co-users** under their own degree coordination (not as a second teaching load for the same professor).

