## 3. Product definition

**vShowroom** — a web platform where fashion designs authored in **CLO 3D** (and any compatible 3D fashion modeller) are exhibited, collected by visitors, and attributed to designers whom visitors can follow. Scoped to the graduates and students of one school, atelier or programme — here: **UDIT Diseño de Moda + UEM Creación Digital**, served by an FE-built runtime.

**Core loop:** designer publishes a piece → visitor browses the showroom → visitor collects a piece → visitor follows the designer → designer sees their collected work.

**Authoring → exhibition pipeline (v1):**

```
CLO 3D (Fashion Design)  ──export──▶  glTF / USDZ / baked stills
         │
         ▼
   vShowroom ingest (FE II)  ──R3F viewer──▶  public piece page + designer attribution
         │
         ▲
CD II avatars / digital looks  ──same ingest contract──┘
```

**Deliberately out of scope** (v1): commerce, payments, real virtual try-on, user-generated 3D authoring in-browser, recommendation algorithms. The showroom **exhibits and attributes**; it does not sell, fit, or personalise. VTON remains an open research problem (IDM-VTON, VTON 360, etc. — authorities §7); students do not "sprint" it.

### Slice map — how it lands on FE II units

| Slice | Unit | Activity type |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Astro shell, routing, content collections for designers/pieces | 2–3 | Lab |
| Offline browsing of a collection; installable | 4 | Lab |
| Test strategy, CI budget, contract test against the data source | 5 | Lab |
| AI-reviewed PR workflow on every merge | 6 | Lab (workflow, not a feature) |
| Performance budget — 3D is heavy, this is where the budget bites | 7 | Lab |
| **R3F viewer** — load and orbit a garment; state in 3D | **8** | Lab |
| **Shader/material work** — fabric appearance, post-processing | **9** | Lab |
| Live data / device or service feed (collections, follows) | 10 | Lab |
| Integration, release, process evidence | 11 | Lab |
| Public exhibition + oral defence | 12 | Evaluación |

**One FE II cohort, one repository, one artefact.** FE I keeps *one repo per student* (individual learning). FE II moves to **one repo per cohort** — with n < 15 this is not a compromise, it is the correct scale for team engineering, and it makes Unit 6's AI-reviewed PR workflow real rather than simulated.

