## 4. Semester choreography — three legs, asynchronous handoff

The calendars do **not** align for live three-way co-teaching:

```
        S1 (Sep–Jan)                    S2 (Feb–Jun)
UDIT    FE II  ██████ builds platform
        FE I   ████████████████████████████████████ (annual — the bridge)
UDIT    Fashion Design ████ CLO + Proyectos / Portfolio feed (year-round studio)
UEM     CD I   ██████ 2D/3D foundations
                                        CD II ██████ avatars · web portfolio · AR
```

**Therefore: asynchronous handoff, not synchronous collaboration.**

| Window | Who | Does |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **S1** | FE II | Builds and releases vShowroom **v1** against *seed* content + any early Fashion Design exports under consent |
| **S1 (parallel)** | Diseño de Moda | Authors garments in **CLO 3D** (Proyectos / digital design spine); volunteers pieces under S1 consent; Y4 **Portfolio** students are the natural first cohort |
| **S1→S2 boundary** | — | **Handoff:** tagged release, deployed URL, contribution guide, open issues, **export contract** (CLO → glTF/stills) |
| **S2** | CD II | Populates with real avatars/designs; **files issues as users**, not as clients |
| **S2** | FE I | Maintains and extends; consumes CD II + Fashion Design issues as authentic backlog |
| **S2+** | Diseño de Moda | Continues feeding pieces; Portfolio / TFG students can treat the live URL as exhibition evidence |

> **Why this is better than co-teaching:** Fashion Design and CD II students become **real users with real CLO/avatar content**, and FE I inherits a **live product with real bug reports** — which no invented brief can manufacture. The temporal offset is a feature.

**Seed content for S1:** FE II cannot wait for CD II. Prefer (in order): (1) consented UDIT Fashion Design CLO exports, (2) the professor's own labelled seed, (3) openly-licensed 3D garment assets. Always label seed vs. cohort content.

**Coordination needed inside UDIT:** Grado en Diseño de Moda coordination — not another teaching assignment for the FE professor. The ask is: *export pathway + consents + optional Portfolio alignment*, not a shared syllabus rewrite.

