## 8. Risks

| Risk | Mitigation |
| --- | --- |
| Two institutions, two ethics regimes (+ third degree inside UDIT) | Start DPO at UDIT **and** UEM **before September**; Fashion Design coordination for S1/S5 consents in parallel; design v1 to need as little as possible (§5) |
| CLO export friction / proprietary formats | Freeze a minimal ingest contract early (glTF + hero still + metadata); document CLO steps for Fashion Design students |
| CD II content arrives after FE II ends | That is the design (§4), not a failure — seed + Fashion Design in S1 |
| Scope inflation ("add try-on!") | §3 out-of-scope list is binding; VTON is an open research problem, not a student sprint |
| One repo, n<15, uneven contribution | Rotating roles + individual exercise channel (forge §2) + oral defence |
| Fashion students' work misused | §5 consents; author retains copyright; revocable |
| Conflating industry prizes with research merit | Keep tracks A/B vs C separate in every proposal (§7.2) |
| Professor bandwidth | FE + CD are one methodology; Fashion Design is **coordination + content**, not a third taught subject for the same load |
| FACTUM deadline mid-semester | Research Note from design, not from results (§7.5) |

